From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: test_freeze: strip absolute --includedir paths from configure args (ILP32)

Debian's test-freeze-strip-libdir.diff drops an absolute --libdir from the
interpreter's CONFIG_ARGS before the test configures and installs a copy of
Python into a private prefix. The ILP32 build also passes an absolute
--includedir (/usr/aarch64-linux-gnu_ilp32/include); sysconfig expands it,
so the test's "make install" tries to write there and fails. Drop it the same
way.
---
 Tools/freeze/test/freeze.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/Tools/freeze/test/freeze.py
+++ b/Tools/freeze/test/freeze.py
@@ -130,4 +130,5 @@
     config_args = shlex.split(sysconfig.get_config_var('CONFIG_ARGS') or '')
     config_args = [arg for arg in config_args if not arg.startswith("--libdir=/")]
+    config_args = [arg for arg in config_args if not arg.startswith("--includedir=/")]
     cmd = [os.path.join(srcdir, 'configure'), *config_args]
     ensure_opt(cmd, 'cache-file', os.path.join(outdir, 'python-config.cache'))
